    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970419.0058\n\nHANOI, April 19 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nSingaporean office project agreed in Ho Chi Minh City\n\n\n\n\nA Singaporean firm has signed a deal to build a 10 million-dollar office complex in Ho Chi Minh City, a report said Saturday.\n\nYuan Cheny Singapore is to take a 70 percent stake in the joint venture project with the Transport Services 3 company, under Vietnam's Ministry of Transport, holding the balance, the Nguoi Lao Dong newspaper said.\n\nThe project is to build a 19-storey office block in central Ho Chi Minh City, due for completion in 1999.",
